        <section class="page-section" id="biography">
            <div class="container">
                <h1 class="page-title animate">About Me</h1>
                <div class="bio-content animate animate-delay-1">
                    <p>
                        I am an industrial management researcher with a strong focus on quality and productivity,
                        AI adoption, and multi-criteria decision-making. My academic journey at the University of
                        Tehran (M.Sc. and B.Sc.) has been shaped by a commitment to bridging rigorous quantitative
                        methods with real-world organizational challenges. I am particularly interested in how
                        emerging technologies — especially AI — can be strategically evaluated and implemented
                        to enhance service quality and operational resilience.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        My research has involved expert-panel methodologies (BWM, TOPSIS), systematic literature
                        reviews, and framework development for banking and manufacturing contexts. I have
                        collaborated with professors and industry partners, and I aim to continue this path
                        through a doctoral program that emphasizes both theoretical depth and practical impact.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

